# Binary permutation offenders

Proposition B.3.2 for degrees five, six, seven, and eight: the exhaustive
best-offender classifications on all four binary permutation sections, their
fixed codimensions, the generated-offender subgroups in a simultaneous Sylow
choice, and the quadratic action ratios. Every hyperplane of `D` is retained;
the regular elementary-eight family occurs only on the degree-eight natural
module. The explicit degree-six lists, strong-offender uniqueness, and
equal-weight inclusions needed by B.3.4 are also re-exported.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*,
1 March 2004 manuscript, printed pp. 83–85.
-/
